==Strategy==
All the enemies have short enough range for [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to do most of the work. In every chapter, you can lure the first LeMurr close to the [[Cat Base]] and save up until you can summon A. Bahamut, then carefully time short-ranged cats like [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Dark Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] so they get hit instead of Bahamut. Once LeMurr is dead, you can safely spam [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] and [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]] like the aforementioned Dark Cat and Crazed Whale Cat, [[Crazed Axe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Brave Cat]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]]. Recommended [[Cat Combo|Combos]] include those with Strong, Unit Attack or Starting Money effects.

==='''Chapter 1'''===
Just let the LeMurr attack the [[Cat Base]] first. Then, send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] when you are ready. Immediately after that, spam [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Dark Cats]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cats]] as meatshields. Artist Cat acts as a tanky support and Dark Cat chips down the first One Horn's health. When the first One Horn is killed, send out your attacking cats to kill the rest of the enemies.

Alternatively, spam [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cats]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cats]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]] and [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cats]].

[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can work as meatshields due to the fact that they are above the cost threshhold.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This stage can be unexpectedly difficult compared to preceding and following stages due to the much stronger enemies and limitations on usual meatshields.

Recommendation is to use level 30 [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], in addition to high-leveled (25-30) [[Crazed Axe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Brave Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]]. Bringing along [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] to add the [[Sunbathers (Combo)|Sunbathers]] Combo is also very useful (having a level 2 [[Worker Cat]] seems to be sufficient for the level). These can be exclusively used to get past the initial LeMurr and One Horns, after which there should be plenty of cash to spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] plus some other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]]/[[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] for good measure.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The hardest part of this stage is stalling until you can kill the first One Horn (it's recommended to bring [[Biohazard (Combo)|Bio]][[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bone]] to help with the consistency of following strategy). Try to hold off LeMurr using [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] until you can burst down One Horn with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. It's difficult to keep One Horn in place, so you will need [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to prevent them from overrunning you. At this point, you can use the inheritance dropped by One Horn to spam your other attackers in [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]], [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]]/[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Alien]] Ubers, etc. It's a straight shot to the finish now.

